    // shorthand builds a non-constructor with dynamic `this`, so `x.toString()` and
    // `Function.prototype.toString.call(x)` both still land on the right receiver.
    //
    // method() cannot be used here: it is declared further down in this same block, so it is in its
    // temporal dead zone at this point, and it would additionally record() the patch for
    // child-realm replay, which this one deliberately does not do. noProtoMethod is already defined
    // above, which is the only helper this needs.
